## Phase 1A: Audit Log System

> **Goal**: Rebuild audit logging (table was created then dropped by `2026_03_06_225703_drop_audit_logs_table.php`). Implement auto-logging for all model changes.

- [ ] **Task 1A.1**: Create new migration `2026_xx_xx_000001_create_audit_logs_table.php` (do NOT rollback the drop migration). Schema: `id` (bigIncrements), `user_id` (foreignId nullable — for system actions), `auditable_type` (string — model class), `auditable_id` (unsignedBigInteger), `event` (string — created/updated/deleted), `old_values` (json nullable), `new_values` (json nullable), `ip_address` (string nullable), `user_agent` (string nullable), `url` (string nullable), `created_at` (timestamp). Add indexes on: `[auditable_type, auditable_id]`, `user_id`, `event`, `created_at`. Do NOT add `updated_at` (audit logs are immutable).

- [ ] **Task 1A.2**: Create `app/Models/AuditLog.php` model. No `$fillable` guard (use `$guarded = []`). Casts: `old_values` → array, `new_values` → array, `created_at` → datetime. Relations: `belongsTo(User)`. Disable timestamps (`public $timestamps = false;` then manually set `created_at` in boot). Add scope `scopeForModel($query, $type, $id)` and `scopeRecent($query, $days = 30)`.

- [ ] **Task 1A.3**: Create `app/Traits/HasAuditLog.php` trait. Use Eloquent model events (`static::created`, `static::updated`, `static::deleted`) in a `bootHasAuditLog()` method. On `created`: log new values (exclude sensitive fields). On `updated`: log old values (original) and new values (changes only, using `$model->getChanges()`). On `deleted`: log old values. Sensitive fields to exclude: `password`, `remember_token`, `no_rekening`, `npwp`. Get current user from `auth()->id()`, IP from `request()->ip()`, user agent from `request()->userAgent()`, URL from `request()->fullUrl()`. Apply this trait to ALL existing models: User, Attendance, Izin, WorkShift, Department, Holiday, LeaveType, SystemSetting, Announcement.

- [ ] **Task 1A.4**: Update `app/Http/Controllers/Admin/AdminAuditLogController.php` (or create if not exists). It should query AuditLog with filters: date range, user, event type, model type. Paginate results (25 per page). Update `resources/views/admin/audit_logs/index.blade.php` to display audit logs in a table with columns: Waktu, User, Aksi, Model, Detail (expandable JSON diff). Add search/filter controls. Use existing pastel-card and pastel-badge components. Ensure route `admin.audit-logs.index` exists and is protected by `permission:view_audit_logs`.

- [ ] **Task 1A.5**: Create `app/Console/Commands/CleanOldAuditLogs.php` artisan command that deletes audit logs older than `audit_log_retention_days` from SystemSetting (default 90 days). Register in `app/Console/Kernel.php` (or `routes/console.php` for Laravel 12) to run daily. Log how many records were deleted.

