## Phase 1C: Violation Points System (Poin Pelanggaran)

> **Goal**: Auto-generate violation points from late attendance, accumulate monthly, trigger warning letters (SP), integrate with future Payroll deductions.

- [ ] **Task 1C.1**: Create migration `2026_xx_xx_000003_create_violation_tables.php`. Three tables: (1) `violation_types`: id, name (string), code (string unique), points (integer), description (text nullable), is_auto (boolean default false — auto-generated vs manual), is_active (boolean default true), timestamps. (2) `violations`: id, user_id (foreignId), violation_type_id (foreignId), tanggal (date), points (integer — snapshot from type), reference_type (string nullable — polymorphic: Attendance, Izin), reference_id (unsignedBigInteger nullable), notes (text nullable), created_by (foreignId nullable — null for auto), timestamps. Indexes: [user_id, tanggal], [reference_type, reference_id]. (3) `warning_letters`: id, user_id (foreignId), type (enum: SP1/SP2/SP3), period_month (string — format YYYY-MM), total_points (integer), issued_at (date), notes (text nullable), created_by (foreignId nullable), timestamps. Unique: [user_id, type, period_month].

- [ ] **Task 1C.2**: Create models: `app/Models/ViolationType.php` (hasMany Violation), `app/Models/Violation.php` (belongsTo User, belongsTo ViolationType, morphTo reference), `app/Models/WarningLetter.php` (belongsTo User). Add `HasAuditLog` trait to all three. Add to User model: `hasMany(Violation)`, `hasMany(WarningLetter)`. Add to Attendance model: `morphMany(Violation, 'reference')`.

- [ ] **Task 1C.3**: Create `database/seeders/ViolationTypeSeeder.php`. Seed default violation types: (1) `TELAT_1` — "Terlambat 1-15 menit", 1 point, is_auto=true, (2) `TELAT_2` — "Terlambat 16-30 menit", 2 points, is_auto=true, (3) `TELAT_3` — "Terlambat 31-60 menit", 3 points, is_auto=true, (4) `TELAT_4` — "Terlambat >60 menit", 5 points, is_auto=true, (5) `ALPHA` — "Tidak hadir tanpa keterangan", 10 points, is_auto=true, (6) `MANUAL` — "Pelanggaran manual", 0 points (admin sets), is_auto=false. Register in DatabaseSeeder.

- [ ] **Task 1C.4**: Create `app/Services/ViolationService.php`. Methods: (1) `generateFromAttendance(Attendance $attendance)`: Calculate late minutes from `jam_masuk` vs shift `start_time` + `late_tolerance_minutes`. Map to violation type (TELAT_1/2/3/4). Create Violation record with reference to Attendance. Skip if violation already exists for this attendance. (2) `generateAlpha(User $user, Carbon $date)`: Create ALPHA violation for user who didn't attend and has no izin. (3) `getMonthlyPoints(User $user, string $yearMonth)`: Sum points for user in given month. (4) `checkWarningThreshold(User $user, string $yearMonth)`: If monthly points ≥10 and no SP1 exists → create SP1. If ≥20 and no SP2 → create SP2. If ≥30 and no SP3 → create SP3. Return created warning letter or null. (5) `getPayrollDeduction(User $user, string $yearMonth)`: Calculate deduction amount based on system setting formula (configurable: per-point flat amount, or percentage of tunjangan kehadiran).

- [ ] **Task 1C.5**: Integrate auto-violation into attendance flow. In `app/Http/Controllers/Api/AttendanceController.php`, after successfully recording a late check-in (where status is 'terlambat'), call `ViolationService::generateFromAttendance($attendance)`. This should happen AFTER the attendance record is saved, not before. Also create `app/Console/Commands/GenerateAlphaViolations.php` artisan command: runs daily at end of work day, finds users who have no attendance AND no approved izin for today, generates ALPHA violations. Register in scheduler to run daily at the configured `auto_checkout_time`.

- [ ] **Task 1C.6**: Add system settings for violation configuration. Create migration to add to `system_settings`: `violation_deduction_type` (enum: per_point/percentage, default 'per_point'), `violation_deduction_per_point` (decimal, default 25000), `violation_deduction_percentage` (decimal, default 0 — percentage of tunjangan kehadiran), `sp1_threshold` (integer, default 10), `sp2_threshold` (integer, default 20), `sp3_threshold` (integer, default 30). Update SystemSetting model with new fields and casts. Add "Poin Pelanggaran" tab in admin settings view.

- [ ] **Task 1C.7**: Create admin views and controller. `app/Http/Controllers/Admin/AdminViolationController.php` with methods: index (list violations with filters: user, date range, type, paginated), show (detail with reference link), create (manual violation form), monthlyReport (summary per user per month with SP status). Views: `resources/views/admin/violations/index.blade.php` (table with pastel-badges for point severity: 1-2=sage, 3-5=peach, 10=rose), `create.blade.php` (form for manual violation), `monthly-report.blade.php` (summary table with SP indicators). Add routes in `routes/web.php` under admin group with new permission `manage_violations`. Update `RoleAndPermissionSeeder` to add `manage_violations` permission to Direktur, VP, Manager. Add sidebar menu item "Poin Pelanggaran" with Material Icon `gavel` under appropriate section.

- [ ] **Task 1C.8**: Add violation summary to employee dashboard. In `resources/views/dashboard.blade.php`, add a small card showing current month's violation points and any active warning letters. Query via `ViolationService::getMonthlyPoints()`. Show as pastel-badge: 0 points = sage "Bersih", 1-9 = peach "Perhatian", 10+ = rose "Peringatan". If SP exists, show SP level badge.

