## Phase 1D: Anti-Fake GPS & Liveness Detection

> **Goal**: Multi-layer anti-cheat system to prevent GPS spoofing and photo-based face recognition bypass.

- [ ] **Task 1D.1**: Create migration `2026_xx_xx_000004_create_employee_devices_table.php`. Schema: `id`, `user_id` (foreignId), `device_fingerprint` (string unique), `device_name` (string nullable — derived from User-Agent), `platform` (string nullable), `browser` (string nullable), `screen_resolution` (string nullable), `is_trusted` (boolean default true), `last_used_at` (timestamp nullable), `created_at`, `updated_at`. Add index on `user_id`. Also add migration to add columns to `attendances` table: `device_fingerprint` (string nullable), `gps_readings` (json nullable — array of 3 lat/long readings), `ip_address` (string nullable), `timezone_client` (string nullable), `anomaly_score` (integer default 0), `anomaly_flags` (json nullable — array of flag strings).

- [ ] **Task 1D.2**: Create `app/Models/EmployeeDevice.php` model. Relations: belongsTo(User). Add HasAuditLog trait. Add to User model: `hasMany(EmployeeDevice)`. Add system settings migration for: `max_devices_per_user` (integer, default 2), `anomaly_score_warning_threshold` (integer, default 30), `anomaly_score_reject_threshold` (integer, default 60), `enable_anti_cheat` (boolean, default true).

- [ ] **Task 1D.3**: Update frontend GPS collection. In `resources/views/dashboard.blade.php`, modify the `cameraHandler()` Alpine.js component. Instead of single `getCurrentPosition()`, collect 3 GPS readings with 2-second intervals. Store all 3 in an array. Also collect: `navigator.userAgent`, `screen.width + 'x' + screen.height`, `Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone`, and a device fingerprint hash (SHA-256 of userAgent + screen + timezone + language). Check if `navigator.geolocation` has mock location indicators (some browsers expose this). Send all data as additional fields in the FormData POST to `/api/attendance/auto`: `gps_readings` (JSON string of 3 readings), `device_fingerprint`, `timezone_client`, `mock_location_detected` (boolean).

- [ ] **Task 1D.4**: Create `app/Services/AntiCheatService.php`. Constructor accepts attendance request data. Method `validate(): AntiCheatResult` runs 6 checks, each returning a score (0-20) and flag string: (1) **GPS Variance Check**: If 3 readings have variance < 0.000001 in both lat/long → suspicious (real GPS always has micro-variance). Score: 15. Flag: `gps_too_stable`. (2) **Speed Anomaly**: Compare current GPS with user's last attendance GPS. Calculate distance/time. If speed > 200 km/h → impossible. Score: 20. Flag: `speed_anomaly`. (3) **Accuracy Paradox**: If GPS accuracy is exactly 1.0 or < 3.0 meters → suspicious (real GPS rarely this precise). Score: 10. Flag: `accuracy_paradox`. (4) **Device Consistency**: Check device_fingerprint against `employee_devices` table. If new device and user already has `max_devices_per_user` trusted devices → flag. Score: 15. Flag: `unknown_device`. (5) **Timezone Mismatch**: Compare client timezone with expected timezone from GPS coordinates (use simple longitude-based calculation: timezone_offset ≈ longitude/15). If mismatch > 2 hours → suspicious. Score: 10. Flag: `timezone_mismatch`. (6) **Mock Location Flag**: If client reports mock_location_detected = true → immediate flag. Score: 20. Flag: `mock_location`. Total anomaly_score = sum of all check scores. Return `AntiCheatResult` DTO with: score, flags array, passed (score < reject_threshold), warning (score >= warning_threshold). Log all checks to audit log.

- [ ] **Task 1D.5**: Integrate AntiCheatService into attendance API. In `app/Http/Controllers/Api/AttendanceController.php`, after GPS validation but before face recognition: (1) If `enable_anti_cheat` system setting is true, instantiate AntiCheatService with request data. (2) Run `validate()`. (3) If not passed (score >= reject_threshold) → return 403 with message "Terdeteksi anomali lokasi. Hubungi admin." and log the attempt. (4) If warning (score >= warning_threshold but < reject_threshold) → allow but save anomaly_score and anomaly_flags to attendance record, send notification to admin. (5) If passed → proceed normally. (6) Always save device_fingerprint, gps_readings, ip_address, timezone_client, anomaly_score, anomaly_flags to the attendance record. (7) Register/update device in employee_devices table.

- [ ] **Task 1D.6**: Implement liveness detection in face-service. In `face-service/face_service.py`, add a new function `check_liveness(image)` that performs: (1) **LBP Texture Analysis**: Convert to grayscale, compute Local Binary Pattern histogram. Real faces have different texture distribution than printed photos/screens. Compare LBP variance — if too low (flat texture) → likely fake. (2) **Reflection Detection**: Check for screen glare patterns — high-intensity spots with specific shape. (3) **Color Distribution**: Real skin has specific color distribution in YCrCb space. Printed photos have different distribution. Return a liveness_score (0.0-1.0) and is_live boolean (threshold 0.5). Integrate into `/recognize_frame` endpoint: before recognition, run liveness check. If `anti_spoofing_enabled` setting is true and is_live is false → return `{"status": "rejected", "message": "Liveness check failed"}`. Add liveness_score to the response.

- [ ] **Task 1D.7**: Create admin anomaly dashboard. Add a section in `resources/views/admin/attendance/index.blade.php` (or new view `anomaly.blade.php`) showing recent attendance records with anomaly_score > 0. Table columns: Karyawan, Waktu, Anomaly Score (color-coded badge: 0=sage, 1-29=sky, 30-59=peach, 60+=rose), Flags (list of flag badges), Device. Add filter by score range. Admin can mark device as untrusted. Add route and controller method. Add "Anomali" sub-menu under Attendance in sidebar.

